  "executive_summary": "This paper reports the first enantioselective total synthesis of madangamine E, a complex pentacyclic marine alkaloid, in 30 steps. The synthesis is enabled by the development of a novel organocatalytic desymmetrizing intramolecular Michael addition reaction. This key transformation converts a prochiral ketone tethered to a β,β'-disubstituted nitroolefin into a chiral bicyclic core with near-perfect enantio- and diastereoselectivity. The reaction efficiently establishes three stereogenic centers, including a quaternary carbon stereocenter, and is highly scalable. The authors utilized density functional theory (DFT) calculations to probe the mechanism, revealing that the enantio-determining step is an irreversible C-C bond formation stabilized by cooperative hydrogen bonding interactions between the thiourea catalyst, the nitro group, and the enamine intermediate. Following the construction of the rigid bicyclic core, the synthesis proceeded through several key steps, including a mild one-pot oxidative lactamization to form the B ring, a two-step Z-selective olefination of a sterically hindered ketone, and two ring-closing metathesis (RCM) reactions to install the macrocyclic D and E rings. The final product was obtained in good yield and its structure was confirmed by comparison with literature data. This work demonstrates the power of catalytic desymmetrization in generating stereochemical complexity from simple achiral precursors, offering a new strategy for the synthesis of complex natural products.",
